{"authored" [{"question" "q-19194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨-2,-1,-4⟩$ and $b=⟨6,-5,3⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 6+(-1)\\cdot (-5)+(-4)\\cdot 3}{{6}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{3}^{2}}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{19}{70}⟨6,-5,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{70}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jak