e/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,0,0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-19194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{70}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $r=⟨-5,1,3⟩$ and $s=⟨n,-2,4⟩.$ Given that the projection of $r$ onto $s$ is the zero vector, find the value of $n.$\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $r$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $s$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\nr⊥s\\,⟹\\,r\\cdot s=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & ={r}_{x}\\cdot {s}_{x}+{r}_{y}\\cdot {s}_{y}+{r}_{z}\\cdot {s}_{z} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot n+1\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5n-2+12 \\\\  & =10-5n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & =0 \\\\ 10-5n & =0 \\\\ n & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7459781824c6f21b40d26082ff3711104219233040a184de8850470e27f22fdf" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/state.json" "file_sha256" "4f8632640fc29664d687e17528e49f8515219b333415e77652836487813d906a" "basis" 815 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13977621/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-19194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨-2,-1,-4⟩$ and $b=⟨6,-5,3⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-19194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}b \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 6+(-1)\\cdot (-5)+(-4)\\cdot 3}{{6}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{3}^{2}}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{19}{70}⟨6,-5,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{70}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-19194" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "517eced771327f4ff05fb744563637545a3dfe6ae65012f5b770c93f1e4e9745"} {"question" "q-19194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-19194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{35}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{70}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{35},-\\frac{57}{35}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-\\frac{57}{70},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{70}⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,0,0⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-19194" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\frac{57}{35},\\frac{19}{14},-\\frac{57}{70}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $r=⟨-5,1,3⟩$ and $s=⟨n,-2,4⟩.$ Given that the projection of $r$ onto $s$ is the zero vector, find the value of $n.$\n\n$n=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $r$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $s$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\nr⊥s\\,⟹\\,r\\cdot s=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & ={r}_{x}\\cdot {s}_{x}+{r}_{y}\\cdot {s}_{y}+{r}_{z}\\cdot {s}_{z} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot n+1\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-5n-2+12 \\\\  & =10-5n.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot s & =0 \\\\ 10-5n & =0 \\\\ n & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "517eced771327f4ff05fb744563637545a3dfe6ae65012f5b770c93f1e4e9745"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-316761" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $r=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$ and $s=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Find the vector projection of $r$ onto $s.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{s}\\,r=⟨$ \n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{s}\\,r & =\\frac{r\\cdot s}{s\\cdot s}s \\\\  & =\\frac{{r}_{x}{s}_{x}+{r}_{y}{s}_{y}+{r}_{z}{s}_{z}}{{s}_{x}^{2}+{s}_{y}^{2}+{s}_{z}^{2}}s \\\\  & =\\frac{(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 0+7\\cdot (-2)}{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}s \\\\  & =\\frac{-17}{5}⟨1,0,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,-\\frac{17}{5},0,\\frac{34}{5}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317655" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "517eced771327f4ff05fb744563637545a3dfe6ae65012f5b770c93f1e4e9745"} {"question" "q-317655" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317655" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{17}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317655" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317655" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317655" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317655" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{34}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $c=⟨-2,1,5⟩$ and $d=⟨4,0,-3⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $d$ onto $c.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{c}\\,d & =\\frac{c\\cdot d}{c\\cdot c}c \\\\  & =\\frac{{c}_{x}{d}_{x}+{c}_{y}{d}_{y}+{c}_{z}{d}_{z}}{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 0+5\\cdot (-3)}{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{-8+0-15}{4+1+25}⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{-23}{30}⟨-2,1,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\,\\frac{23}{15},-\\frac{23}{30},-\\frac{23}{6}\\,⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317658" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "517eced771327f4ff05fb744563637545a3dfe6ae65012f5b770c93f1e4e9745"} {"question" "q-317658" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317658" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{23}{15}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317658" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317658" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{23}{30}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317658" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317658" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{23}{6}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=t\\,i+4j-k$ and $b=2i-j.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $t.$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"question" "q-317943" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular.\n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =t\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2t-4+0 \\\\  & =2t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2t-4 & =0 \\\\ 2t & =4 \\\\ t & =2 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14071264/state.json" "file_sha256" "3c9039a57d69b2501c15eed4e2fd1d7e1902a6cb5e0f5c14e146a80d969e920e"} {"questi